A freely moving particle follows a spacetime geodesic. In differential form, using an affine parameter $\lambda$, $\frac{d^2x^\mu}{d\lambda^2}
+\Gamma^\mu{}_{\rho\sigma}
\frac{dx^\rho}{d\lambda}
\frac{dx^\sigma}{d\lambda}=0.$ The connection tells the tangent how to remain parallel to itself as the particle moves.

