Indeed, near the horizon $\frac{dt}{dr}
\sim-\frac{1}{1-r_s/r}
=-\frac{r}{r-r_s}.$ Its integral diverges logarithmically. This proves the infinite Schwarzschild-time statement without implying an infinite reading on the falling clock.

